@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
title git post-commit — format, then lint
' purpose: why a commit still runs fmt and lint after HEAD moves, and how the hook is installed without git config
' covers: mise.toml
' covers: .golangci.yml
' covers: internal/contract/git_hooks_test.go
' covers: internal/contract/comment_blocks_test.go
' `mise run lint` is a run array in mise.toml. Its gates, in order:
'   1 go test of TestEveryTrackedGoFileIsGofmted and
'     TestNoCommentBlockOverThreeLines (internal/contract): go/format over every
'     tracked .go file, whatever its build tags, and the comment-block rule (N14,
'     _spec/_conventions/spec-conventions.puml)
'   2 go vet ./..., go vet -tags=image ./internal/imagetest/, go vet -tags=e2e
'     ./e2e/ (the e2e vet joined 2026-11-10 so `mise run ci` compiles the tmux pins)
'   3 golangci-lint run, with build-tags [image, e2e] in .golangci.yml
' So a post-commit hook also reports comment blocks over three lines and
' unformatted e2e files, after the fact like every other lint finding.
' The two contract tests also run in test-go, baseline and ci.
'
' ── THE HOOK (2026-11-12) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
' `mise run install-git-hooks` runs `mise generate git-pre-commit --hook
' post-commit --task post-commit --write`. mise writes an untracked #!/bin/sh
' hook that execs `mise run post-commit`, moves an existing hook to
' post-commit.old, and in a linked worktree writes the common .git/hooks
' (MEASURED on mise 2026.10.17; a worktree commit fired it).
' The hidden [tasks.post-commit] runs [{ task = "fmt" }, { task = "lint" }].
' Its skip_if reads SKIP_GIT_HOOKS through `get_env | trim | lower in [...]`
' with envflag.On's words, so 1, true, yes, on, enable and enabled skip it.
' Pinned by internal/contract/git_hooks_test.go:
'   TestPostCommitRunsFormatThenLint
'   TestPostCommitSkipIfSpeaksTheEnvflagWords
'   TestMiseDeclaresInstallGitHooks
' A clone that never ran install-git-hooks has no hook; one installed before
' 2026-11-12 holds the old shim and needs the task run once. Until then every
' commit prints a go run error, which git ignores for post-commit.
' CONTRIBUTING.md names the step (TestMiseDeclaresInstallGitHooks).
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.

participant "git commit" as COMMIT <<app>>
participant ".git/hooks/post-commit\n(mise's, untracked)" as HOOK <<app>>
participant "mise run post-commit\n(hidden, skip_if)" as BODY <<app>>
participant "mise run fmt" as FMT <<app>>
participant "mise run lint" as LINT <<app>>
participant "mise run install-git-hooks" as INST <<app>>

COMMIT ARROW_MAIN HOOK : HEAD already advanced
HOOK ARROW_MAIN BODY : exec mise run post-commit
BODY ARROW_MAIN FMT : { task = "fmt" }
FMT ARROW_MAIN LINT : format first so lint sees it
INST ARROW_OPTIONAL HOOK : mise generate git-pre-commit

note right of HOOK
  **HEAD is already written.** This hook
  cannot change the commit. Format may
  dirty the tree; lint failing prints
  after the fact.
end note

note over INST
  **No git config.** core.hooksPath is
  not set. mise writes the hook into
  git's hooks dir, so a clone still
  needs one command:
  mise run install-git-hooks.
end note

note right of FMT
  **Format before lint.** Lint's first
  gate is the gofmt test. Running lint
  first would fail the files fmt is
  about to rewrite. The hook does not
  git add or git commit.
end note

note right of BODY
  **SKIP_GIT_HOOKS keeps its name.**
  skip_if reads it with envflag's
  on-words, so CI skips both tasks
  and "0" still runs them.
end note
@enduml
